# Motor models with a non-ideal actuator, for identifying the real robot.
#
# `SimpleMotor` applies the commanded torque exactly. The real drive does not:
# it has a torque constant below the assumed one, a dead band that small
# commands never leave, and a Coulomb friction. `NonidealTorque` carries those
# 3 as fitted parameters, and the motors and closed loops below wrap it the same
# way the ideal ones wrap `SimpleMotor`, so the two can be compared directly.
#
# The calibration scripts in calibration/ fit `k_scale`, `db` and `tau_c`
# together with the plant's inertias and friction to a robot run.

"""
The real actuator: a torque-constant error, a dead band, and a friction that is
LARGER AT REST THAN IN MOTION.

`tau = k_scale * (tau_cmd - db * tanh(tau_cmd / db)) - f(w) * tanh(w / w_eps)`

with the Stribeck friction

`f(w) = tau_c + (tau_s - tau_c) * exp(-(w / w_s)^2)`

so the friction is `tau_s` at rest and falls to `tau_c` once the wheel slides.

WHY THE VELOCITY DEPENDENCE IS NECESSARY. With `tau_s = tau_c` this reduces to
the earlier model, whose friction was the same at every speed. That model cannot
fit the robot. Swept against a 165 s run on 2026-09-18, with everything else
held at its fitted value:

    db [duty]   position RMS [cm]   peak |x| [cm]   (robot 15.8)
      0.010          1.230              16.0
      0.030          1.849              16.7
      0.050          2.978              17.8
      0.077          4.463              19.1   <- the measured break-away
      0.100          5.123              19.7

Monotonic, with no minimum anywhere near the bench value of 0.077 to 0.122 duty.
The direction gives the reason away: a stickier robot should fall SHORT, and
this one sails FURTHER past. A friction that does not depend on speed charges
the full static break-away while the wheel is spinning, so the model cannot
brake. The fit escapes by choosing `db = 0.010 duty`, 8 times below the
measured value, because most of the samples are in the sweep and not in the
holds. That number is therefore not a measurement of the dead band; it is the
least-damaging compromise available to a model of the wrong shape.

What this still does NOT capture is true hysteresis: break-away depending on the
history of approach, and presliding displacement. That needs an internal state,
as in LuGre. `tanh(w / w_eps)` also means the wheel never quite sticks, it
creeps very slowly, so `w_eps` must be small for the holds to look right.
"""
component NonidealTorque
  tau_cmd = RealInput() {^tau_cmd}
  w = RealInput() {^w}
  tau = RealOutput() {^tau}
  "Torque-constant error (1 = ideal)"
  parameter k_scale::Real = 0.85
  "Dead-band width, N*m"
  parameter db::Real = 0.01
  "Coulomb friction torque in motion, N*m"
  parameter tau_c::Real = 0.005
  "Static friction torque at rest, N*m. Equal to tau_c disables the Stribeck term."
  parameter tau_s::Real = 0.005
  "Stribeck speed: how fast the friction falls from tau_s to tau_c, rad/s"
  parameter w_s::Real = 0.1
  "Speed scale of the friction smoothing, rad/s"
  parameter w_eps::Real = 0.5
relations
  tau = k_scale * (tau_cmd - db * tanh(tau_cmd / db)) - (tau_c + (tau_s - tau_c) * exp(-(w / w_s)^2)) * tanh(w / w_eps)
metadata {
  "Dyad": {"icons": {"default": "dyad://BlockComponents/Gain.svg"}}
}
end

"Planar motor with the `NonidealTorque` actuator model. Plays the real robot in the synthetic study."
component NonidealMotor
  extends MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.PartialTwoFrames
  torquesource = RotationalComponents.Sources.TorqueSource() {^torquesource}
  motor_rotation = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.Revolute(render = false) {^motor_rotation}
  damper = RotationalComponents.Components.Damper(d = d) {^damper}
  fixed = RotationalComponents.Components.Fixed() {^fixed}
  speed = RotationalComponents.Sensors.VelocitySensor() {^speed}
  actuator = NonidealTorque(k_scale = k_scale, db = db, tau_c = tau_c, tau_s = tau_s, w_s = w_s, w_eps = w_eps) {^actuator}
  "Torque command"
  torqueinput = RealInput() {^torqueinput}
  "Viscous friction coefficient"
  parameter d::RotationalDampingConstant = 0.0
  parameter k_scale::Real = 0.85
  parameter db::Real = 0.01
  parameter tau_c::Real = 0.005
  parameter tau_s::Real = 0.005
  parameter w_s::Real = 0.1
  parameter w_eps::Real = 0.5
relations
  connect(torquesource.spline, motor_rotation.flange_a, damper.spline_a, speed.spline) {^id1}
  connect(frame_a, motor_rotation.frame_a) {^id2}
  connect(motor_rotation.frame_b, frame_b) {^id3}
  connect(torquesource.support, damper.spline_b, fixed.spline) {^id4}
  connect(torqueinput, actuator.tau_cmd) {^id5}
  connect(speed.w, actuator.w) {^id6}
  connect(actuator.tau, torquesource.tau) {^id7}
metadata {
  "Dyad": {"icons": {"default": "dyad://MultibodyComponents/Revolute.svg"}}
}
end

"`PlanarDyadBot` with the `NonidealMotor`: the synthetic 'real robot'."
component NonidealPlanarDyadBot
  wheelJoint = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.OneDOFRollingWheelJoint(radius = R) {^wheelJoint}
  wheelinertia = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.Body(I = Iw, radius = 0.01, m = m, phi(initial = 0.0), w(initial = 0.0)) {^wheelinertia}
  motor = NonidealMotor(d = d, k_scale = k_scale, db = db, tau_c = tau_c, tau_s = tau_s, w_s = w_s) {^motor}
  body_mass = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.BodyShape(color = [0.2, 0.2, 0.2, 0.9], r = [0, 2 * L], r_cm = [0, L], m = M, I = Ib, radius = 0.03, body(w(initial = 0.0))) {^body_mass}
  IMU = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.AbsolutePosition(resolve_in_frame = MultibodyComponents.ResolveInFrame.World()) {^IMU}
  torque = RealInput() {^torque}
  x = RealOutput() {^x}
  theta = RealOutput() {^theta}
  x_dot = RealOutput() {^x_dot}
  theta_dot = RealOutput() {^theta_dot}
  parameter M::Mass = 0.1
  parameter m::Mass = 0.05
  parameter R::Length = 0.04
  parameter L::Length = 0.08
  parameter Ib::Inertia = 2.5e-4
  parameter Iw::Inertia = 1e-4
  parameter d::RotationalDampingConstant = 0.0001
  parameter phi0::Angle = 0.0
  parameter k_scale::Real = 0.85
  parameter db::Real = 0.01
  parameter tau_c::Real = 0.005
  parameter tau_s::Real = 0.005
  parameter w_s::Real = 0.1
relations
  initial body_mass.body.phi = phi0
  connect(wheelinertia.frame_a, wheelJoint.frame_a) {^id11}
  connect(motor.frame_b, wheelJoint.frame_a) {^id12}
  connect(motor.frame_a, IMU.frame_a, body_mass.frame_a) {^id13}
  connect(torque, motor.torqueinput) {^id14}
  x = IMU.x
  theta = IMU.phi
  x_dot = wheelJoint.v
  theta_dot = body_mass.body.w
metadata {
  "Dyad": {"icons": {"default": "dyad://DyadBotComponents/PlanarDyadBot.svg"}}
}
end

"""
`DiscreteCascadeControlledDyadBot` with the nonideal plant.
Makes the synthetic robot log: the 200 Hz controller balances the robot with
the actuator defects it does not know about.
"""
component NonidealCascadeDyadBot
  extends CascadeControllerParams
  world = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.World(g = 9.82, nominal_length = 0.1) {^world}
  plant = NonidealPlanarDyadBot(phi0 = phi0) {^plant}
  square = BlockComponents.Sources.Square(amplitude = 0.05, frequency = 1 / 10) {^square}
  firstorder = BlockComponents.Continuous.FirstOrder(T = 0.1) {^firstorder}
  firstorder1 = BlockComponents.Continuous.FirstOrder(T = 0.1) {^firstorder1}
  controller = DiscreteCascadeController(k_angle = k_angle, Ti_angle = Ti_angle, Td_angle = Td_angle, k_pos = k_pos, Ti_pos = Ti_pos, Td_pos = Td_pos, Ts = Ts) {^controller}
  parameter phi0::Angle = 0.1
  structural parameter Ts::Real = 0.005
relations
  initial firstorder.x = 0.0
  initial firstorder1.x = 0.0
  connect(square.y, firstorder.u) {^id7}
  connect(firstorder.y, firstorder1.u) {^id8}
  connect(plant.x, controller.pos_measurement) {^id9}
  connect(plant.theta, controller.angle_measurement) {^id10}
  connect(plant.torque, controller.torque) {^id11}
  connect(firstorder1.y, controller.pos_reference) {^id12}
metadata {
  "Dyad": {
    "tests": {"case1": {"stop": 20}},
    "icons": {"default": "dyad://DyadBotComponents/PlanarDyadBot.svg"}
  }
}
end

"Synthetic robot run: 20 s of the nonideal robot under the cascade controller, one square-wave period of the position reference."
analysis NonidealCascadeDyadBotTransient
  extends TransientAnalysis(stop = 20, abstol = 1e-8, reltol = 1e-8)
  model = NonidealCascadeDyadBot()
end

"""
Cascade-controlled robot with the nonideal actuator and the position reference as
an input. Made for fitting the actuator to a robot run: drive `pos_reference` with
the reference the robot logged, and fit `k_scale`, `db`, `tau_c` of the actuator
together with the plant's inertias and friction, and `theta_bias`, the offset of
the tilt estimate that the controller balances around (a bias makes the robot
park at `theta_bias / k_pos` from the reference).
"""
component NonidealReferenceDyadBot
  extends CascadeControllerParams
  world = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.World(g = 9.82, nominal_length = 0.1) {^world}
  plant = NonidealPlanarDyadBot(phi0 = phi0) {^plant}
  controller = CascadeController(k_angle = k_angle, Ti_angle = Ti_angle, Td_angle = Td_angle, k_pos = k_pos, Ti_pos = Ti_pos, Td_pos = Td_pos) {^controller}
  "Adds the tilt-measurement bias to the true tilt"
  tilt_sum = BlockComponents.Math.Add() {^tilt_sum}
  bias_source = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = theta_bias) {^bias_source}
  "Position reference"
  pos_reference = RealInput() {^pos_reference}
  parameter phi0::Angle = 0.0
  "Bias of the tilt that the controller sees, rad. Stands for the estimator offset from the gyro bias and the angle_zero error. Zero is a perfect measurement."
  parameter theta_bias::Real = 0.0
relations
  connect(controller.torque, plant.torque) {^id1}
  connect(plant.theta, tilt_sum.u1) {^id2}
  connect(bias_source.y, tilt_sum.u2) {^id5}
  connect(tilt_sum.y, controller.angle_measurement) {^id6}
  connect(plant.x, controller.pos_measurement) {^id3}
  connect(pos_reference, controller.pos_reference) {^id4}
metadata {
  "Dyad": {"icons": {"default": "dyad://DyadBotComponents/PlanarDyadBot.svg"}}
}
end
